Found under k328 (apply worker, 2026-10-31), state lane, an edge case: a CoreDNS Corefile with no root server block but with its own registry.local block -- since k328 configure_registry_dns warns (no root block to add the host to), while OCP::Drift reports no registry.local drift. The writer and the drift check read the Corefile differently.

Cleanup alongside: the Corefile nesting-depth loop now exists three times (corefile_with_host, corefile_drop_added_hosts, corefile_has_root_block in Apply/Network.pm or Registry.pm) -- one parser would keep the writer and OCP::Drift reading it the same way.

Done = writer and drift agree on that Corefile (test), one shared block parser.

